\includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{figures/paper/fig_entropy_layers.pdf}
\caption{Per-layer attention entropy ratio for SmolVLA (16 layers) and OpenVLA (32 layers). SmolVLA maintains near-uniform entropy across all layers (range 0.92\textendash 0.98, total variation 0.06), confirming that pixel-shuffle tokens resist selective attention at every processing depth. OpenVLA exhibits progressive sharpening from layer 0 (0.98) to layer 29 (0.48), with total variation 0.50. Selectivity begins at layer 2 (ratio 0.80), indicating that MLP-projected tokens are semantically distinguishable enough for spatial selection after minimal self-attention.}
\label{fig:entropy_layers}
\end{figure}

All measurements use real LIBERO data (SmolVLA: 2400 rollout frames for overall entropy, 256 frames for per-layer analysis; OpenVLA: 250 frames), ensuring the comparison reflects task-relevant visual inputs rather than random noise.

